export const READ_ALOUD_QUESTIONS = [
  { id: '1', text: "The park is a pleasant place for people to enjoy nature. It has many green trees, colourful flowers and open spaces. Families often visit the park at weekends. Children can play on the grass while adults relax on benches. Keeping parks clean helps protect plants and animals and makes the local area more beautiful." },
  { id: '2', text: "Drinking enough water every day is important for good health. Our bodies need water to work properly, especially when the weather is hot. People should try to drink water regularly throughout the day. Fresh water is a better choice than sugary drinks. A healthy daily routine can help people feel active and comfortable." },
  { id: '3', text: "Public transport helps people travel around towns and cities. Many passengers use the bus to go to work, school or local shops. Bus stops are usually placed near homes and important buildings. A regular bus service makes daily travel easier. It can also help reduce the number of cars on busy roads." },
  { id: '4', text: "Fresh fruit is an important part of a healthy diet. Many people buy apples, oranges and bananas at their local market. Markets often offer a wide choice of seasonal food. Some customers visit early in the morning to find the freshest products. Eating fruit regularly can provide the body with important vitamins." },
  { id: '5', text: "The weather can change quickly during the day. Heavy rain may arrive in the afternoon, even when the morning is sunny. People should check the weather before leaving home. Carrying an umbrella can be useful during the rainy season. Weather forecasts help families plan their journeys and decide what clothes to wear." },
  { id: '6', text: "Mobile phones are useful tools in everyday life. People use them to make calls, send messages and find information. Before going on a long trip, it is important to charge the phone. A full battery allows travellers to contact family members and use maps when needed. Technology makes many daily activities easier." },
  { id: '7', text: "Many tourists visit popular cities during the summer holidays. They enjoy seeing famous buildings, visiting museums and trying local food. Some people travel with their families, while others prefer to explore alone. Busy tourist areas can become crowded during this season. Planning a journey early can help visitors enjoy their holiday." },
  { id: '8', text: "Some birds travel to warmer countries when winter arrives. They leave places where food becomes difficult to find and temperatures become very low. These journeys can cover long distances across different countries. When the weather becomes warmer again, many birds return to their usual homes. Bird migration is an interesting part of nature." },
  { id: '9', text: "Many people work in small family businesses. These businesses may include shops, restaurants or local services. Family members often share different responsibilities during the working day. Some people serve customers, while others manage money or prepare products. Working together can help a small business succeed and support the local community." },
  { id: '10', text: "A local hospital provides important services for people in the community. Doctors and nurses help patients who are sick or injured. Hospitals need to be ready to provide care every day, including weekends and public holidays. People should know where their nearest hospital is. Good healthcare services help keep communities safe and healthy." },
  { id: '11', text: "The price of vegetables can change from week to week. Farmers may produce less food when the weather is poor. This can make some vegetables more expensive in local shops and markets. Many families compare prices before they buy their groceries. Planning meals and making a shopping list can also help people save money." },
  { id: '12', text: "Walking every morning is a simple way to stay active. People can walk around their neighbourhood, visit a nearby park or enjoy a quiet street. Regular walking helps the body become stronger and supports good health. It can also improve mood and reduce stress. Even a short walk each day can be useful." },
  { id: '13', text: "Saving electricity at home is important for the environment and for family budgets. People can use less energy by switching off lights when they leave a room. They should also turn off televisions and other devices when they are not being used. Small changes in daily habits can reduce electricity use over time." },
  { id: '14', text: "People use messages to stay in contact with family and friends. A short message can share news, make plans or ask an important question. Yesterday, a woman sent a message to her friend about their weekend meeting. Clear communication helps people understand each other. Mobile phones make it easier to stay connected." },
  { id: '15', text: "A river can play an important role in the life of a town. It may flow through parks, gardens and areas where people live. Some residents enjoy walking beside the water, while others visit to watch birds and wildlife. Keeping rivers clean protects nature and helps make the town a pleasant place to live." },
  { id: '16', text: "Many cities are planting more trees to improve the quality of the air. Trees provide shade on hot days and make streets more attractive. They also create places where birds and other small animals can live. Local communities often help by caring for young trees. These projects can make towns healthier and more pleasant for everyone." },
  { id: '17', text: "Regular exercise can help reduce the risk of several common diseases. Activities such as walking, swimming and cycling keep the body active and support heart health. People do not need to spend hours at the gym to enjoy these benefits. A simple exercise routine, followed several times each week, can make a positive difference." },
  { id: '18', text: "Online banking allows customers to manage their money without visiting a bank branch. People can check their account balance, pay bills and transfer money using a computer or mobile phone. These services are convenient for people with busy schedules. However, customers should protect their personal information and use secure passwords when accessing their accounts." },
  { id: '19', text: "The cost of travelling abroad can depend on several factors, including the time of year and the destination. Flights and hotels are often more expensive during school holidays because many families travel together. People who plan their journeys early may find better prices. Comparing different travel options can also help visitors manage their holiday budget." },
  { id: '20', text: "Many people prefer flexible working hours because they have responsibilities outside the workplace. Some employees need time to care for children, attend appointments or support family members. Flexible schedules can help workers organise their daily activities more effectively. Employers may also benefit because staff who have a better work-life balance can feel more motivated." },
  { id: '21', text: "Local farmers play an important role in supplying fresh food to nearby communities. They grow vegetables, fruit and other products that are sold directly to customers. Buying local produce can reduce the distance food travels before reaching shops and markets. It also helps support farming families and encourages people to learn more about where their food comes from." },
  { id: '22', text: "Traffic congestion has become a serious problem in many large cities. During busy periods, thousands of cars and buses travel along the same roads. This can make journeys much longer and increase air pollution. Some cities are improving public transport and encouraging people to walk or cycle. These changes may help reduce pressure on crowded roads." },
  { id: '23', text: "Scientists use special equipment to study changes in the atmosphere. They collect information about temperature, rainfall, wind and other weather conditions. By examining these measurements over time, researchers can identify important patterns. Their findings help people understand changes in the natural environment and improve the accuracy of weather forecasts." },
  { id: '24', text: "Community activities can help people develop stronger relationships with their neighbours. Local events, sports clubs and volunteer projects bring together people of different ages and backgrounds. Taking part in these activities gives residents an opportunity to share experiences and learn new skills. A strong community can make people feel more connected and supported." },
  { id: '25', text: "The price of basic goods has increased in many countries over recent years. Families may find that food, transport and household supplies cost more than they did before. When prices rise, people often need to plan their spending more carefully. Understanding household expenses can help individuals make sensible financial decisions and manage their available money." },
  { id: '26', text: "Social media has changed the way people share information and communicate with others. Users can publish photographs, discuss current events and stay connected with friends who live far away. However, not every message shared online is accurate. People should check information carefully before believing it or passing it on to other users." },
  { id: '27', text: "Some families decide to move to smaller homes because the cost of living has increased. A smaller property may require less money for rent, electricity and general maintenance. Although moving can be difficult, it may help a family manage its monthly expenses. Choosing a suitable home involves considering both personal needs and financial circumstances." },
  { id: '28', text: "Traditional festivals attract visitors from many different parts of the world. These celebrations often include music, dancing, special food and colourful decorations. They give local communities an opportunity to share their customs and history with others. Visitors can learn about different ways of life while enjoying activities that bring people together." },
  { id: '29', text: "Solar panels can produce electricity using energy from the sun. They are often installed on the roofs of houses, schools and office buildings. Unlike some traditional energy sources, solar power does not produce direct air pollution while generating electricity. As technology improves, solar panels are becoming a more practical choice for many households." },
  { id: '30', text: "Clear communication is important in every workplace. Employees need to understand their responsibilities, share information and discuss problems with their colleagues. When instructions are confusing, mistakes and misunderstandings can occur. Listening carefully and asking questions when necessary can improve cooperation. Good communication helps teams complete their work more efficiently and achieve shared goals." },
  { id: '31', text: "Universities are offering more online courses to help students who live far from major cities. These programmes allow learners to attend classes, complete assignments and communicate with teachers through digital platforms. Students can often study at times that suit their schedules. However, successful online learning requires good organisation and regular access to the internet." },
  { id: '32', text: "Governments need to introduce effective policies to reduce pollution from factories and industrial activities. Some companies release harmful substances into the air and water, which can damage the natural environment. Clear regulations encourage businesses to use cleaner methods of production. Regular inspections are also important to ensure that environmental standards are followed." },
  { id: '33', text: "Advances in artificial intelligence are changing the way businesses operate. Computer systems can now analyse large amounts of information, answer customer questions and assist employees with everyday tasks. These developments may help companies save time and improve their services. However, businesses must also consider how new technology affects workers and protects private information." },
  { id: '34', text: "A balanced diet and regular exercise are important for maintaining good health over time. Eating different types of food provides the body with nutrients needed for energy and growth. Physical activity helps strengthen muscles and supports the heart. People who develop healthy habits early in life may find it easier to maintain them as they grow older." },
  { id: '35', text: "Rising living costs have placed additional pressure on households with limited incomes. Families may need to spend more money on food, transport, electricity and housing than they did in previous years. As a result, some people have less money available for savings or leisure activities. Careful budgeting can help households manage their expenses." },
  { id: '36', text: "Employers often consider practical experience as important as formal academic qualifications when selecting new staff. A person who has worked in a particular industry may understand its daily challenges and responsibilities. However, education can provide valuable knowledge and professional skills. Many organisations look for candidates who combine relevant experience with a willingness to continue learning." },
  { id: '37', text: "Researchers are studying how environmental changes affect marine life in oceans and coastal areas. Rising water temperatures, pollution and changes in ocean conditions can influence the behaviour of many species. Scientists collect information from different locations to understand these effects. Their findings may help governments and communities protect marine environments and manage natural resources more responsibly." },
  { id: '38', text: "Improving public transport could help reduce traffic congestion in major cities. When buses and trains are reliable, more people may choose to leave their cars at home. This can reduce the number of vehicles on busy roads and make journeys more efficient. Better transport connections also allow people to reach workplaces, schools and public services more easily." },
  { id: '39', text: "Access to quality education is still unequal in many parts of the world. Children in some communities have modern classrooms, trained teachers and reliable learning materials, while others have very limited resources. These differences can affect future employment opportunities and personal development. Improving educational access is an important step towards creating a fairer society." },
  { id: '40', text: "Small businesses often find it difficult to compete with large international companies. Bigger organisations may have more money for advertising, advanced technology and product development. However, smaller businesses can offer personal service and build strong relationships with local customers. By understanding their customers and managing resources carefully, they can develop a successful place in the market." },
  { id: '41', text: "Extreme weather events are creating serious challenges for communities living near the coast. Strong storms, heavy rainfall and rising sea levels can damage homes, roads and public facilities. Some residents may be forced to leave their properties when conditions become dangerous. Local authorities need to prepare emergency plans and improve protection for vulnerable areas." },
  { id: '42', text: "International travel gives people the opportunity to experience customs and traditions that may be different from their own. Visitors can learn about local food, music, celebrations and everyday lifestyles. These experiences can improve understanding between people from different backgrounds. Travelling also encourages individuals to become more open-minded and appreciate the variety of cultures around the world." },
  { id: '43', text: "News organisations have an important responsibility to provide accurate and balanced information. Journalists should check their facts carefully and consider different viewpoints before publishing a story. Incorrect reporting can confuse the public and damage trust in the media. Readers also need to think critically about the information they receive, especially when news spreads quickly online." },
  { id: '44', text: "Rapid urbanisation has increased the demand for affordable housing in many cities. As more people move into urban areas, local governments must find ways to provide suitable homes and public services. New developments can create additional living space, but they also require careful planning. Good urban design should consider transport, green spaces and the needs of local residents." },
  { id: '45', text: "Scientific discoveries can lead to improvements in many areas of everyday life. New research may help develop better medicines, improve communication systems or create more efficient ways to produce energy. However, discoveries often require years of careful investigation and testing before they become widely available. Scientific progress depends on accurate evidence and continued cooperation between researchers." },
  { id: '46', text: "Public investment in education can support the long-term development of a country's economy. Well-funded schools and universities help students gain the knowledge and skills needed for future employment. Education can also encourage innovation and improve productivity across different industries. Governments therefore need to consider educational spending as an important investment in future generations." },
  { id: '47', text: "Effective teamwork depends on mutual respect and a clear understanding of individual responsibilities. Team members need to share information, listen to different opinions and complete their tasks on time. When people communicate openly, they can often solve problems before they become more serious. Good cooperation allows a group to work towards common goals more successfully." },
  { id: '48', text: "Renewable energy sources are becoming increasingly important in national energy strategies. Solar panels, wind turbines and hydroelectric systems can produce electricity without relying entirely on fossil fuels. Many governments are investing in these technologies to reduce pollution and improve energy security. However, reliable storage and suitable infrastructure are still necessary to support wider use." },
  { id: '49', text: "International trade has created new opportunities for businesses and consumers around the world. Companies can sell their products in overseas markets, while customers have access to a wider range of goods. Trade can also encourage investment and create employment. However, businesses must understand different regulations, customer expectations and cultural practices when entering foreign markets." },
  { id: '50', text: "People's decisions are often influenced by their personal experiences and social environment. Family members, friends and colleagues can affect the way individuals think about different situations. Previous experiences may also influence how someone responds to unfamiliar challenges. Understanding these influences can help explain why people sometimes make different decisions even when they receive the same information." },
  { id: '51', text: "Group discussions are an important part of many educational programmes. Students have opportunities to explain their opinions, listen to different viewpoints and respond to questions from their classmates. These activities can improve confidence and develop critical thinking skills. Teachers also use discussions to check whether learners understand difficult subjects and can apply their knowledge to practical situations." },
  { id: '52', text: "Natural habitats provide essential conditions for the survival of plants and animals. Forests, wetlands and coastal areas support a wide variety of species, many of which depend on specific environmental conditions. When these habitats are destroyed or damaged, biodiversity can decline. Protecting natural environments is therefore important for maintaining ecological balance and preserving wildlife for future generations." },
  { id: '53', text: "Digital platforms have transformed the way organisations communicate with their customers. Businesses can now provide information, answer questions and receive feedback through websites and mobile applications. These services allow companies to respond more quickly to customer needs. However, organisations must ensure that their communication systems are reliable and that personal information is handled responsibly." },
  { id: '54', text: "Medical researchers continue to investigate the long-term effects of insufficient sleep. Studies suggest that regularly sleeping for too few hours may affect concentration, memory and general physical health. Sleep is also important for the body's ability to recover after daily activities. Understanding these effects can help people develop healthier routines and recognise the importance of sufficient rest." },
  { id: '55', text: "Changes in international markets can have a significant impact on local businesses. When the prices of imported materials increase, companies may face higher production costs. Businesses that depend on overseas customers can also be affected by changes in demand or currency values. Understanding international economic conditions helps organisations prepare for uncertainty and make more informed decisions." },
  { id: '56', text: "Professional development programmes help employees respond to changing demands in the workplace. Training courses can introduce new technical skills, improve communication and prepare staff for additional responsibilities. Some organisations provide regular learning opportunities to help their employees remain competitive. Investing in professional development can benefit both workers and employers by improving performance and supporting career progression." },
  { id: '57', text: "Ocean temperatures influence weather patterns across many regions of the world. Changes in sea temperature can affect evaporation, rainfall and the movement of large weather systems. Scientists use satellites, research vessels and monitoring equipment to collect information about the oceans. By examining these patterns, researchers can improve their understanding of climate conditions and possible environmental changes." },
  { id: '58', text: "Reliable public transport can improve people's access to employment opportunities. Workers who live far from business districts may depend on buses and trains to reach their workplaces. When services are frequent and affordable, travelling becomes more manageable. Better transport connections can also support local economic activity by allowing businesses to attract employees from a wider area." },
  { id: '59', text: "Social inequality can affect people's access to essential services such as education and healthcare. Individuals living in disadvantaged communities may have fewer opportunities to improve their living conditions. These differences can continue across generations if they are not addressed. Governments and community organisations can help by improving public services and supporting people who face economic or social difficulties." },
  { id: '60', text: "Before introducing a new product, companies need to understand the behaviour and expectations of their customers. Market research can reveal which features people value and how much they are prepared to pay. Businesses can use this information to improve product design and advertising. A clear understanding of customer needs reduces uncertainty and helps companies compete more effectively." },
  { id: '61', text: "Rising sea levels present serious challenges for communities located in low-lying coastal regions. Higher water levels can increase the risk of flooding, damage buildings and affect important transport routes. Some areas may also experience changes in groundwater and agricultural conditions. Local authorities need to consider long-term protection measures to reduce the risks faced by residents and businesses." },
  { id: '62', text: "Cultural exchange allows people to learn about traditions, beliefs and lifestyles from different parts of the world. Students who study abroad, for example, often experience new customs and develop friendships with people from other backgrounds. These experiences can challenge existing assumptions and encourage greater understanding. Cultural exchange can therefore contribute to stronger relationships between communities." },
  { id: '63', text: "The rapid spread of information online has made it increasingly important to evaluate news sources carefully. Articles and photographs can be shared with thousands of people within a short period, even when the information has not been verified. Readers should consider who published a report and whether reliable evidence supports its claims. Responsible information sharing helps reduce the influence of misleading content." },
  { id: '64', text: "City planners must consider population growth when designing future housing and transport systems. As urban areas become more crowded, demand for homes, schools and public facilities increases. Poor planning can create traffic congestion and place pressure on existing services. Effective development requires cooperation between government departments, private organisations and local residents to create practical long-term solutions." },
  { id: '65', text: "Researchers often combine different methods to obtain more reliable evidence. Surveys can provide information about people's opinions, while interviews may offer a deeper understanding of individual experiences. Scientific measurements can also help identify patterns that are difficult to observe directly. By comparing information from several sources, researchers can develop stronger conclusions and recognise possible weaknesses in their findings." },
  { id: '66', text: "Effective public policies should address immediate concerns while also considering the long-term needs of society. For example, governments may need to respond quickly to rising living costs while developing plans to improve education and healthcare. These decisions often involve limited financial resources and competing priorities. Careful planning can help ensure that public investment produces lasting benefits." },
  { id: '67', text: "Misunderstandings can occur when people interpret the same message in different ways. Differences in language, experience and cultural background may influence how information is received. In professional environments, unclear instructions can lead to mistakes and delays. Asking questions, listening carefully and confirming important details can reduce confusion and improve cooperation between colleagues." },
  { id: '68', text: "Governments are encouraging households and businesses to reduce their dependence on fossil fuels. Energy-efficient equipment, renewable electricity and improved building design can all contribute to lower energy consumption. These changes may require an initial financial investment, but they can provide savings over time. Reducing fossil fuel use can also support efforts to limit environmental damage and air pollution." },
  { id: '69', text: "International cooperation is necessary when countries face challenges that extend beyond their national borders. Issues such as climate change, disease outbreaks and economic instability can affect several regions at the same time. Governments may need to share information, coordinate policies and provide assistance to one another. Working together can make it easier to respond to problems that individual countries cannot solve alone." },
  { id: '70', text: "Personal motivation can influence how individuals respond to difficult situations and unexpected setbacks. Some people remain focused on their goals when problems arise, while others may lose confidence and delay taking action. Previous experiences and available support can affect these responses. Understanding the role of motivation can help people develop strategies for managing challenges and maintaining progress." },
  { id: '71', text: "Academic success often depends on how effectively students manage their time. Learners who organise their schedules can balance classroom activities, independent study and personal responsibilities. Setting realistic goals also helps students monitor their progress. Although studying regularly requires discipline, good time management can reduce unnecessary stress and improve the quality of learning." },
  { id: '72', text: "Deforestation contributes to climate change and threatens the survival of many animal and plant species. Forests absorb carbon dioxide and provide habitats for a wide range of wildlife. When large areas of woodland are removed, these natural benefits are reduced. Protecting forests and managing land responsibly are important steps towards maintaining environmental stability." },
  { id: '73', text: "Businesses increasingly depend on digital systems to store information and improve their daily operations. These systems allow employees to organise records, communicate with colleagues and access important documents more efficiently. However, companies must protect their information against security threats. Regular software updates and appropriate staff training can reduce the risk of data loss and unauthorised access." },
  { id: '74', text: "Regular medical check-ups can help identify potential health problems before they become serious. Doctors may recommend routine examinations to monitor blood pressure, cholesterol levels and other important indicators. Early detection can allow patients to receive treatment sooner and make necessary lifestyle changes. Preventative healthcare therefore plays an important role in maintaining long-term wellbeing." },
  { id: '75', text: "Economic uncertainty may discourage companies from investing in new projects. When businesses are unsure about future costs, customer demand or government policies, they may delay important decisions. This can affect employment and slow economic growth. Clear information and stable economic conditions can help organisations plan more confidently and make decisions about future investment." },
  { id: '76', text: "Employees who communicate effectively are often better prepared to resolve workplace conflicts. Differences of opinion are common when people have different responsibilities and expectations. Listening carefully and explaining concerns respectfully can prevent small disagreements from becoming larger problems. Managers can also support positive working relationships by encouraging open discussions and treating employees fairly." },
  { id: '77', text: "Scientists are developing new techniques to monitor pollution in rivers and coastal waters. Modern equipment can measure the concentration of harmful substances and identify changes in water quality. This information helps researchers understand how pollution affects aquatic plants and animals. Governments can use the findings to improve environmental regulations and protect important water resources." },
  { id: '78', text: "Expanding railway networks could provide a more sustainable alternative to private vehicles. Trains can carry large numbers of passengers using less road space than individual cars. Reliable railway services may also reduce traffic congestion and improve connections between towns and cities. However, building new railway infrastructure requires careful planning, substantial investment and consideration of local communities." },
  { id: '79', text: "Population growth can place considerable pressure on public services and infrastructure. As communities become larger, demand for schools, hospitals, housing and transport may increase. Local authorities must plan carefully to ensure that essential services remain available to residents. Investment in infrastructure can support growing populations and help maintain a suitable standard of living." },
  { id: '80', text: "Understanding market trends allows companies to make more informed business decisions. Changes in customer preferences, technology and economic conditions can create both opportunities and risks. Businesses that regularly examine market information may be better prepared to adjust their products and services. Careful planning helps organisations respond to competition and maintain their position in the marketplace." },
  { id: '81', text: "Changes in rainfall patterns can affect agricultural production and food security. Some farming regions may experience longer periods without rain, while others face heavy rainfall and flooding. These conditions can damage crops and make it more difficult for farmers to plan their activities. Understanding changing weather patterns helps communities prepare for potential difficulties in food production." },
  { id: '82', text: "Preserving historical buildings helps future generations understand their cultural heritage. Old buildings often reflect the architectural styles, materials and traditions of the communities that created them. Some have served important purposes in local history, including education, government and public gatherings. Restoration projects can protect these structures while allowing people to continue learning from the past." },
  { id: '83', text: "Online advertising has changed the relationship between businesses and their target audiences. Companies can use digital platforms to display advertisements to people who may be interested in particular products or services. This approach allows businesses to reach specific groups more directly. However, consumers are becoming increasingly aware of how their personal information may be used for advertising." },
  { id: '84', text: "Poorly planned urban development can create traffic problems and reduce access to green spaces. When new housing areas are built without suitable roads, public transport and recreational facilities, residents may experience difficulties in their daily lives. Parks and open spaces are also important for health and community activities. Successful urban planning must balance growth with environmental and social needs." },
  { id: '85', text: "The reliability of research findings depends partly on the quality of the information collected. If data is incomplete or inaccurate, the conclusions drawn from a study may be misleading. Researchers must therefore use appropriate methods and carefully examine their results. Repeating investigations and comparing findings with other studies can help establish greater confidence in scientific evidence." },
  { id: '86', text: "Local authorities need to balance economic development with the protection of public spaces. New commercial projects can create jobs and increase business activity, but they may also affect parks and community facilities. Residents should have opportunities to express their views before major changes are approved. Careful planning can help ensure that development benefits the wider community." },
  { id: '87', text: "Listening carefully to different viewpoints can lead to more productive discussions. People may have different experiences and priorities, even when they are discussing the same issue. Giving others time to explain their opinions can improve understanding and reduce unnecessary disagreement. Respectful communication does not require everyone to agree, but it allows people to consider alternative ideas." },
  { id: '88', text: "Improvements in battery technology could make renewable energy more reliable and accessible. Solar and wind power depend on natural conditions, which means electricity production can change throughout the day. Better batteries can store additional energy when production is high and release it when demand increases. This technology may help communities make greater use of renewable electricity." },
  { id: '89', text: "International partnerships allow universities to share knowledge and conduct collaborative research. Academics from different countries can combine their expertise, compare findings and develop new approaches to complex problems. Students may also benefit from exchange programmes and opportunities to study abroad. These partnerships encourage cooperation and help educational institutions contribute to scientific and social progress." },
  { id: '90', text: "People's attitudes towards change are often shaped by their previous experiences and expectations. Someone who has benefited from a new opportunity may be more willing to accept future changes. Others may feel uncertain when familiar routines are replaced. Understanding these reactions can help organisations introduce new ideas more effectively and provide support during periods of adjustment." },
  { id: '91', text: "Universities are increasingly encouraging students to develop skills beyond their main area of study. Employers often value communication, problem-solving and the ability to work independently. Although academic knowledge remains essential, students who can apply what they have learned to practical situations may find it easier to adapt to changing professional environments." },
  { id: '92', text: "Protecting natural habitats requires cooperation between governments, local communities and environmental organisations. When forests and wetlands are damaged, many species lose the conditions they need to survive. Conservation projects can help restore these areas, but their success often depends on long-term planning and the responsible use of natural resources." },
  { id: '93', text: "Artificial intelligence is changing the way organisations manage information and make decisions. Automated systems can analyse large amounts of data much faster than traditional methods. However, their results still need careful human supervision, particularly when decisions affect people's employment, finances or access to important public services." },
  { id: '94', text: "Maintaining good health involves more than responding to illness when symptoms appear. Regular physical activity, balanced nutrition and sufficient sleep all contribute to long-term wellbeing. Medical professionals also recommend preventive examinations because identifying potential problems early can improve treatment outcomes and reduce the likelihood of serious complications." },
  { id: '95', text: "Changes in interest rates can influence the financial decisions of households and businesses. When borrowing becomes more expensive, families may postpone major purchases, while companies might delay expansion plans. These individual decisions can gradually affect consumer spending, investment and the wider performance of the national economy." },
  { id: '96', text: "Professional development is becoming increasingly important as industries respond to technological and economic changes. Employees who regularly update their knowledge may be better prepared for new responsibilities. Employers can support this process by providing practical training, encouraging collaboration and creating opportunities for workers to develop their existing abilities." },
  { id: '97', text: "Scientific discoveries often depend on researchers examining evidence from several different perspectives. A result that initially appears convincing may require further investigation before reliable conclusions can be reached. Repeating experiments and allowing other scientists to examine the findings helps strengthen confidence in the research and reduces the risk of misleading interpretations." },
  { id: '98', text: "Efficient public transport can improve access to employment, education and essential services. However, expanding a transport network requires careful consideration of population growth, financial resources and environmental impact. Planners must also ensure that different services connect effectively, allowing passengers to complete their journeys without unnecessary delays." },
  { id: '99', text: "Social inequality can affect people's opportunities throughout their lives. Differences in family income, educational access and living conditions may influence the choices available to individuals. Addressing these challenges requires more than temporary assistance, as lasting improvements often depend on policies that create fairer opportunities across different communities." },
  { id: '100', text: "Companies operating in competitive markets must understand both customer expectations and changes in consumer behaviour. Businesses that rely entirely on previous success may struggle when new competitors introduce better products or services. Regular market research can help organisations recognise emerging demands and make informed decisions about their future direction." },
  { id: '101', text: "Rising global temperatures are affecting weather patterns in many regions. Some areas experience longer periods of drought, while others face heavier rainfall and an increased risk of flooding. These changes create difficulties for agriculture, infrastructure and public safety, making climate adaptation an important priority for governments and local communities." },
  { id: '102', text: "Cultural traditions often reflect the history and shared experiences of a community. As younger generations encounter different lifestyles and influences, some traditional practices may gradually disappear. Museums, educational programmes and community events can help preserve this heritage while allowing people to understand how cultural identities continue to develop." },
  { id: '103', text: "The rapid spread of digital media has changed how people receive and evaluate information. News can reach large audiences within minutes, but speed does not always guarantee accuracy. Readers therefore need to consider the reliability of their sources, examine supporting evidence and avoid sharing claims that have not been properly verified." },
  { id: '104', text: "Modern cities must balance the demand for new housing with the need to maintain comfortable and healthy living environments. High-density development can make better use of limited land, but poorly planned construction may increase congestion and reduce access to public spaces. Effective urban planning considers these competing priorities together." },
  { id: '105', text: "Research findings can influence important decisions in medicine, education and public policy. However, the usefulness of a study depends on the quality of its methods and the reliability of the information collected. Researchers must explain their procedures clearly so that others can assess the evidence and determine whether the conclusions are justified." },
  { id: '106', text: "Public spending decisions often involve difficult choices because governments have limited financial resources. Investment in healthcare, education and transport may all be necessary, yet each programme requires careful evaluation. Officials must consider immediate public needs while also ensuring that current spending supports the country's long-term development." },
  { id: '107', text: "Effective communication requires more than expressing ideas clearly. People must also consider the knowledge, expectations and perspectives of their audience. In professional situations, misunderstandings can arise when important details are assumed rather than explained. Asking appropriate questions and confirming key information can prevent unnecessary confusion." },
  { id: '108', text: "Renewable energy sources are becoming increasingly important as countries attempt to reduce their dependence on fossil fuels. However, solar and wind power do not always produce electricity at the exact moment it is needed. Improved energy storage systems and more flexible electricity networks can help address this challenge." },
  { id: '109', text: "International cooperation allows countries to exchange knowledge, develop new technologies and respond to challenges that extend beyond national borders. Although global partnerships can create economic opportunities, they may also increase competition between industries. Successful cooperation therefore requires clear agreements and an understanding of each country's responsibilities." },
  { id: '110', text: "People do not always make decisions through careful examination of available evidence. Previous experiences, emotional reactions and personal expectations can influence how information is interpreted. Understanding these psychological factors helps explain why individuals sometimes reach different conclusions, even when they are presented with exactly the same information." },
  { id: '111', text: "Access to higher education can influence both individual opportunities and the development of society. However, students from disadvantaged backgrounds may face financial and practical barriers that affect their ability to continue studying. Scholarships and flexible learning programmes can reduce some of these difficulties, although wider improvements in educational access require sustained institutional support." },
  { id: '112', text: "The protection of endangered species depends on understanding the environmental conditions that support their survival. Habitat destruction, pollution and illegal hunting can reduce wildlife populations over time. Conservation programmes are more effective when scientific research is combined with local knowledge and when communities have a genuine opportunity to participate in protecting their natural surroundings." },
  { id: '113', text: "The increasing use of digital platforms has transformed the way organisations store, exchange and analyse information. Although these systems improve efficiency, they also create responsibilities relating to privacy and data protection. Companies must establish reliable security procedures and ensure that employees understand how sensitive information should be handled." },
  { id: '114', text: "Public health campaigns are designed to encourage behaviours that reduce the risk of preventable diseases. Their effectiveness depends partly on whether information is communicated clearly and reaches the people who need it most. When communities understand the reasons behind health recommendations, they may be more willing to adopt healthier habits." },
  { id: '115', text: "Inflation can reduce the purchasing power of households, particularly when the cost of essential goods rises faster than wages. Families may respond by changing their spending habits or postponing non-essential purchases. Policymakers must carefully consider these pressures because measures intended to control inflation can also influence employment and economic growth." },
  { id: '116', text: "Flexible working arrangements have become more common as organisations reconsider how professional responsibilities should be managed. Remote work can reduce commuting time and provide greater independence, but it may also weaken informal communication between colleagues. Employers need to establish clear expectations while ensuring that employees remain connected to their teams." },
  { id: '117', text: "Advances in medical science have made it possible to identify certain diseases before serious symptoms develop. Researchers are investigating how genetic information and biological indicators can improve early diagnosis. Nevertheless, scientific progress must be accompanied by careful ethical consideration, particularly when personal medical information is collected and analysed." },
  { id: '118', text: "The development of electric vehicles is changing the automotive industry, but their widespread adoption depends on more than improvements in battery performance. Charging facilities must be accessible, electricity supplies need to be reliable, and vehicles must remain affordable. Governments and manufacturers therefore have important roles in supporting the transition." },
  { id: '119', text: "An ageing population creates challenges for healthcare systems, pension programmes and the wider economy. As life expectancy increases, governments must consider how public services can remain sustainable while meeting the needs of older citizens. Encouraging healthy ageing and supporting people who wish to remain economically active may help address some of these pressures." },
  { id: '120', text: "A company's reputation can influence customer confidence long before a purchase is made. Businesses that respond honestly to complaints and communicate their policies clearly are more likely to establish lasting relationships with consumers. However, maintaining a positive reputation requires consistent behaviour rather than occasional promotional campaigns or attractive public statements." },
  { id: '121', text: "Climate change is creating additional uncertainty for communities that depend heavily on agriculture. Unpredictable rainfall and rising temperatures can affect planting schedules, crop quality and the availability of water. Farmers may need to adopt different techniques, while governments can support adaptation through research, improved infrastructure and access to reliable information." },
  { id: '122', text: "Cultural exchange can encourage people to reconsider assumptions about unfamiliar societies. Through international education, travel and artistic collaboration, individuals gain opportunities to experience different perspectives. Although misunderstandings may arise when traditions are interpreted without sufficient context, respectful discussion can strengthen mutual understanding and create lasting connections between communities." },
  { id: '123', text: "Media organisations face increasing pressure to attract attention while maintaining professional standards. Sensational headlines may generate immediate interest, but they can also distort the significance of an event. Responsible journalism requires accurate reporting, appropriate context and a willingness to distinguish verified information from speculation or personal opinion." },
  { id: '124', text: "Urban regeneration projects aim to improve neglected areas through investment in housing, transport and public facilities. While redevelopment can create employment and attract new businesses, it may also increase property prices and displace existing residents. Successful projects should therefore consider the needs of established communities rather than focusing exclusively on economic growth." },
  { id: '125', text: "Long-term research projects often require substantial financial support and cooperation between different institutions. Their findings may take years to produce practical benefits, making it difficult to measure success immediately. Nevertheless, sustained investigation can reveal patterns that short studies overlook and provide evidence for decisions affecting future generations." },
  { id: '126', text: "Government policies are more likely to succeed when they are based on reliable evidence and an understanding of public needs. However, proposed changes may affect different groups in unequal ways. Consulting communities before implementation allows officials to identify potential difficulties and adjust their approach before problems become more widespread." },
  { id: '127', text: "Communication across different cultures requires awareness of how language, gestures and social expectations influence meaning. A phrase considered polite in one setting may appear unusually direct in another. Developing cultural sensitivity helps people avoid unnecessary misunderstandings and communicate more effectively in international workplaces and educational environments." },
  { id: '128', text: "The transition towards cleaner energy requires significant investment in electricity generation, storage and distribution. Renewable sources can reduce environmental damage, but their output may vary according to weather conditions. A dependable energy system therefore needs a combination of technologies, supported by effective planning and long-term investment." },
  { id: '129', text: "Global supply chains allow businesses to obtain materials and components from different parts of the world. This arrangement can reduce costs and increase production capacity, but it also creates dependence on international transport and stable trading relationships. Disruptions in one region may consequently affect manufacturers and consumers across several countries." },
  { id: '130', text: "Motivation is influenced by a combination of personal goals, social expectations and previous experiences. Individuals may remain committed to difficult tasks when they understand the purpose of their efforts and recognise gradual progress. However, excessive pressure can reduce confidence, suggesting that encouragement and realistic expectations are important for sustained performance." },
  { id: '131', text: "The effectiveness of higher education should not be measured exclusively by examination results or graduate employment statistics. Universities also have a responsibility to cultivate intellectual independence, encourage critical enquiry and expose students to competing perspectives. An educational environment that prioritises genuine understanding over the accumulation of qualifications is more likely to prepare graduates for complex professional and social responsibilities." },
  { id: '132', text: "Environmental degradation frequently results from the cumulative effects of activities that appear relatively insignificant when considered individually. Agricultural expansion, industrial pollution and excessive resource consumption can gradually undermine the resilience of entire ecosystems. Addressing these pressures requires coordinated intervention, particularly because environmental damage may become extremely difficult or prohibitively expensive to reverse once critical ecological thresholds have been exceeded." },
  { id: '133', text: "Technological innovation often develops more rapidly than the legal and ethical frameworks intended to regulate its consequences. Artificial intelligence, for example, offers substantial opportunities to improve productivity, yet its widespread application raises questions about accountability, transparency and human oversight. Policymakers must therefore establish principles that encourage innovation without allowing commercial interests to undermine fundamental public protections." },
  { id: '134', text: "The relationship between physical and psychological health is considerably more complex than traditional medical approaches sometimes suggest. Chronic stress can influence immune function, sleep quality and the management of existing conditions. Consequently, effective healthcare increasingly recognises the importance of addressing patients' social circumstances and emotional wellbeing alongside the clinical symptoms that initially brought them to medical attention." },
  { id: '135', text: "Economic prosperity does not necessarily translate into an equivalent improvement in living standards for every section of society. Although national income may increase, unequal distribution can prevent substantial parts of the population from benefiting from that growth. Economists therefore examine a broader range of indicators, including employment security, access to essential services and changes in household purchasing power." },
  { id: '136', text: "The transformation of professional occupations is challenging established assumptions about job security and career progression. As automation replaces certain routine responsibilities, employees are increasingly expected to demonstrate adaptability, sound judgement and transferable expertise. Organisations that invest in continuous professional development may be better positioned to manage this transition while retaining valuable institutional knowledge." },
  { id: '137', text: "Scientific understanding advances through the continual examination of existing explanations rather than the unquestioning acceptance of established conclusions. Researchers must remain prepared to revise their interpretations when new evidence contradicts previous assumptions. This process of critical reassessment is fundamental to scientific progress, although communicating uncertainty accurately can be difficult when public audiences expect definitive answers." },
  { id: '138', text: "The long-term sustainability of urban transport depends on integrating infrastructure development with broader environmental and economic objectives. Expanding road capacity may temporarily relieve congestion, but it can also encourage greater dependence on private vehicles. A more comprehensive strategy considers public transport accessibility, pedestrian safety and land-use planning as interconnected elements of an efficient metropolitan system." },
  { id: '139', text: "Social cohesion can deteriorate when economic disadvantage becomes closely associated with limited access to education, employment and political representation. Although individual circumstances differ, persistent structural barriers may reinforce divisions between communities. Meaningful social progress therefore requires institutions to examine not only immediate inequalities but also the underlying arrangements that allow disadvantage to continue across generations." },
  { id: '140', text: "Corporate success increasingly depends on balancing short-term commercial performance with long-term organisational resilience. Businesses that pursue immediate profitability without considering environmental responsibilities, employee welfare or changing consumer expectations may expose themselves to significant reputational and financial risks. Strategic decision-making consequently requires a broader assessment of value than conventional financial indicators alone can provide." },
  { id: '141', text: "Climate adaptation is increasingly recognised as an indispensable complement to emissions reduction, particularly in regions already experiencing irreversible environmental changes. Nevertheless, adaptation strategies can inadvertently reinforce existing inequalities when their benefits are distributed according to financial capacity rather than vulnerability. Effective policy must therefore reconcile ecological necessity with social justice, ensuring that communities least responsible for environmental degradation are not disproportionately burdened by its consequences." },
  { id: '142', text: "Cultural preservation involves a delicate negotiation between continuity and transformation. Attempts to protect inherited traditions may inadvertently freeze them into forms that no longer reflect the communities sustaining them. Conversely, unrestricted commercialisation can diminish their historical significance. Meaningful preservation therefore depends on recognising cultural identity as something continually interpreted and reconstructed rather than merely inherited unchanged." },
  { id: '143', text: "The personalisation of digital content has fundamentally altered the relationship between information providers and their audiences. Recommendation systems can increase relevance by anticipating individual interests, yet they may simultaneously narrow exposure to unfamiliar perspectives. This tension raises important questions about intellectual independence, algorithmic accountability and whether convenience should take precedence over the diversity of information essential to informed democratic participation." },
  { id: '144', text: "Urban resilience cannot be achieved through infrastructure investment alone, since a city's capacity to withstand disruption is also determined by institutional coordination and social preparedness. Technically sophisticated developments may remain vulnerable if essential services are inaccessible to disadvantaged populations. Consequently, effective planning must integrate physical durability with equitable resource distribution and the institutional flexibility required to respond to unforeseen circumstances." },
  { id: '145', text: "The credibility of academic research depends not merely on methodological sophistication but also on the transparency with which uncertainty and limitations are acknowledged. Selective reporting can create an exaggerated impression of certainty, particularly when inconclusive findings receive less attention than statistically significant results. Scientific integrity therefore requires researchers to distinguish robust evidence from provisional interpretation, even when doing so complicates their original hypotheses." },
  { id: '146', text: "Effective governance frequently requires reconciling objectives that are individually defensible but collectively difficult to accommodate. Policies designed to accelerate economic growth may conflict with environmental safeguards, while extensive regulation can impose disproportionate costs on smaller enterprises. Rather than assuming that one objective should invariably prevail, responsible institutions must evaluate competing consequences transparently and remain accountable for the compromises they introduce." },
  { id: '147', text: "Meaningful dialogue depends on recognising that disagreement does not necessarily indicate a failure of communication. Participants may interpret identical evidence differently because their underlying assumptions, experiences and priorities are not the same. Constructive discussion therefore requires more than persuasive expression; it demands intellectual humility, careful listening and a willingness to reconsider conclusions when alternative interpretations are supported by credible evidence." },
  { id: '148', text: "The decarbonisation of electricity systems presents a complex coordination problem involving technological innovation, market incentives and regulatory reform. Although renewable generation is becoming increasingly cost-effective, its variability introduces challenges that cannot be resolved through additional generating capacity alone. Long-term reliability depends on integrating storage, demand management and interconnected networks within an institutional framework capable of anticipating changing patterns of consumption." },
  { id: '149', text: "Economic interdependence has enabled unprecedented levels of international cooperation, yet it has also exposed national economies to disruptions originating far beyond their borders. Attempts to strengthen domestic resilience through greater self-sufficiency may reduce certain vulnerabilities while sacrificing the efficiencies created by international specialisation. Policymakers must therefore distinguish strategic dependence from unnecessary exposure rather than treating global integration as inherently beneficial or harmful." },
  { id: '150', text: "Human judgement is frequently influenced by cognitive shortcuts that simplify complex decisions but can also produce systematic distortions. Individuals may assign excessive importance to information that confirms existing beliefs while overlooking evidence that challenges them. Recognising these tendencies does not eliminate bias, but it can encourage more deliberate reasoning, particularly when decisions carry significant personal, professional or societal consequences." },
];
